<section class="voting-info-card" aria-labelledby="voting-info-heading">
  <h2 id="voting-info-heading">When + how to vote</h2>

  <div class="vi-grid">

    <div class="vi-block">
      <div class="vi-eyebrow">Election Day</div>
      <div class="vi-headline">Tuesday, May 19, 2026</div>
      <div class="vi-detail">6:00 AM – 6:00 PM</div>
      <div class="vi-note">Hardin uses a vote-center model: <strong>any registered voter can use any of the 15 locations</strong> below.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="vi-block">
      <div class="vi-eyebrow">Early voting (no excuse)</div>
      <div class="vi-headline">Thu May 14 · Fri May 15 · Sat May 16</div>
      <div class="vi-detail">8:00 AM – 4:30 PM</div>
      <div class="vi-note">Two locations only: <strong>Hardin County Clerk's Office</strong> (E-town) + <strong>Colvin Community Center</strong> (Radcliff). No reason needed.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="vi-block">
      <div class="vi-eyebrow">Excused early in-person</div>
      <div class="vi-headline">May 6 – 13 (business days)</div>
      <div class="vi-detail">8:00 AM – 4:30 PM</div>
      <div class="vi-note">Clerk's office only. Requires a qualifying reason (work, military, medical, etc.).</div>
    </div>

    <div class="vi-block vi-warn">
      <div class="vi-eyebrow">Mail-in absentee — closed</div>
      <div class="vi-headline">Request portal closed May 5</div>
      <div class="vi-note">Already-mailed ballots must be returned by 6:00 PM 5/19. If you didn't request one, vote in person.</div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="vi-row vi-row-actions">
    <a class="vi-action" href="https://vrsws.sos.ky.gov/VIC/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      <span class="vi-action-icon">🗳️</span>
      <span class="vi-action-text">
        <strong>Am I registered?</strong>
        <span>Check your status at the KY Voter Information Center</span>
      </span>
    </a>
    <a class="vi-action" href="https://hccoky.org/pdf/ballots/26PComp.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      <span class="vi-action-icon">📄</span>
      <span class="vi-action-text">
        <strong>Official sample ballot</strong>
        <span>2026 primary composite (PDF, all races county-wide)</span>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <details class="vi-details">
    <summary>What to bring + closed-primary rules</summary>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Photo ID</strong> — Kentucky driver's license, KY photo ID, U.S. passport, military ID, or a few other government-issued options. If you don't have one, you can sign an affirmation at the polls.</li>
      <li><strong>Closed primary</strong> — Kentucky only lets you vote in your registered party's primary. Independents and "no party" voters get a ballot with nonpartisan races only (city races, school board) on May 19. Voter registration closed April 20, 2026.</li>
      <li><strong>Help available</strong> — every polling place is required to provide accessibility assistance and language help if you ask.</li>
    </ul>
  </details>
</section>
